<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2653" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱρετ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that may be taken</i> or <i>conquered</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόλῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.201
				</span></i>
			; <i>to be understood</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				81b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱρέομαι</span>) <i>to be chosen, eligible</i>,
			opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φευκτός</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phlb.</u>
				21d
			</span></i> sq., <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1097a32
			</span></i>, etc.: freq. in 
				Comp.
			 or 
				Sup.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.126
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				156
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζόης πονηρᾶς θάνατος αἱρετώτερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					401
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>chosen, elected</i>, esp. opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κληρωτός</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				12.154
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				759b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1294b9
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				915c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.13
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ. βασιλῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Mx.</u>
					238d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυραννίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1285a31
				</span></i>
			:—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ. ἄνδρες</span>
			<i>commissioners</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lyc.</u>
				26
			</span></i>. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ αἱ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				1.3.21
			</span></i>: = Lat.<i>optiones</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyd.
				<u>Mag.</u>
				1.46
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>that may be chosen</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱρετέος</span> (q.v.), <i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				3.22
			</span></i>.</div>
